      {
        "title": "Substitution",
        "body": "With $u=x^3-3x$, $du=3(x^2-1)dx$, and the limits become $u=0$ to $u=2$. (Here $u^{4/3}=(\\sqrt[3]{u})^4$ is the real power; $u$ is negative on part of the range.) The integral is $\\frac13\\left[\\frac{3}{7}u^{7/3}\\right]_0^2=\\frac17\\,2^{7/3}$.\n\n**Answer: $\\frac{2^{7/3}}{7}$**"
      }
