    "prompt": "Evaluate $\\displaystyle\\int_0^1\\binom{22}{20}x^2(1-x)^{20}\\,dx$.",
    "image": null,
    "choices": null,
    "answer": "1/23",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Beta integral",
        "body": "$\\int_0^1x^2(1-x)^{20}dx=B(3,21)=\\frac{2!\\,20!}{23!}$ and $\\binom{22}{20}=\\frac{22!}{2!\\,20!}$, so the product is $\\frac{22!}{23!}=\\frac1{23}$.\n\n**Answer: $\\frac1{23}$**"
      },
      {
        "title": "Expand",
        "body": "$\\binom{22}{20}=231$. With $u=1-x$ the integral is $231\\int_0^1(1-2u+u^2)u^{20}du=231\\left(\\frac1{21}-\\frac1{11}+\\frac1{23}\\right)=11-21+\\frac{231}{23}=-10+10+\\frac1{23}=\\frac1{23}$.\n\n**Answer: $\\frac1{23}$**"
      }
    ],
