        "title": "Substitute $u=\\ln x$",
        "body": "With $u=\\ln x$, $x=e^u$, $dx=e^udu$ and $x^{\\ln x-1}=e^{u(u-1)}$: the integrand becomes $e^{u^2-u}\\cdot u\\cdot e^u=ue^{u^2}$. So the integral is $\\int_0^1ue^{u^2}du=\\frac{e-1}2$.\n\n**Answer: $\\frac{e-1}2$**"
