        "body": "With $x=e^u$: $I=\\int_{-\\infty}^\\pi e^u\\sin u\\,du$. Since $\\frac d{du}\\left[\\frac{e^u(\\sin u-\\cos u)}2\\right]=e^u\\sin u$,\n$$I=\\left[\\frac{e^u(\\sin u-\\cos u)}2\\right]_{-\\infty}^{\\pi}=\\frac{e^\\pi\\,(0+1)}2=\\frac{e^\\pi}2.$$\n\n**Answer: $\\frac{e^\\pi}2$**"
